      "message": "fix(2d): enter a dead-end later Outside pass by a ramp along the pass\n\nA later pass of a 2D Offset \"Pass starts at: Outside\" plan can start at a\ndead end of a split level. No lead chord reaches it from cleared stock, so\nthe tool disc meets the crescent of uncut stock at the full tool width.\nMain enters by a helix or a plunge there. The pin\noutside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock reads 332.88 mm2 of\nstock cut by those later entries.\n\nEnter such a start by the existing zig-zag ramp along the pass (3 degrees\nby default), so the tool lowers while it travels the first cut. The helix\nand the plunge stay the entry at every other start. The late-entry pin now\ncounts only plunges and helices: a ramp along the pass is a gradual entry.\nThe pin reads 0.00 mm2.\n\nFixes #3567\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
